menu "WiFi Dap OTA module (module 5, WP-205)"

    config BIRDIEBOT_OTA_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the OTA JSON module 5 (GET_INFO / GET_PROGRESS / ABORT)"
        default n
        help
            Registers the OTA module (id 5) on the existing WS/API JSON routers
            through API_JSON_MODULE_REGISTER.

            Slim build (A2, 2026-10-26): default n because the Web OTA upload
            feature is disabled (CONFIG_BIRDIEBOT_WEB_OTA_UPLOAD_ENABLE);
            module 5 then answers nothing.  Set to y together with the upload
            endpoint to restore the full OTA feature
            (docs/feature-flags.md A2).  The OTA partition table, bootloader
            rollback configuration and the rollback helpers
            (wt_ota_mark_app_valid()) stay enabled either way: main/ still
            confirms a pending-verify image after boot.

    config BIRDIEBOT_OTA_BUF_SIZE
        int "HTTP upload receive chunk size (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 512 16384
        help
            Static receive buffer size used by uri_ota.c (WP-206) for
            httpd_req_recv(). docs/ota-local-upload.md §3.2 requires a static
            buffer (~4096 B), never a 3 MB heap allocation.

    config BIRDIEBOT_OTA_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Upload idle timeout (ms)"
        default 10000
        range 1000 600000
        help
            docs/ota-local-upload.md §3.3: no body bytes for this long ->
            esp_ota_abort() + state ERROR("upload timeout") + HTTP 408.

    config BIRDIEBOT_OTA_MAX_DURATION_MS
        int "Maximum upload session duration (ms)"
        default 300000
        range 10000 3600000
        help
            docs/ota-local-upload.md §3.3: total session cap from
            esp_ota_begin(); exceeding it aborts the session the same way.

    config BIRDIEBOT_OTA_AUTO_MARK_VALID
        bool "Automatically confirm a pending-verify OTA image after boot"
        default n
        help
            When CONFIG_BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE=y, an OTA-updated image
            boots in ESP_OTA_IMG_PENDING_VERIFY and must be confirmed by the
            application. The preferred integration is for main/app_main to call
            wt_ota_mark_app_valid() from a single 10 s timer after WiFi, the
            webserver and the DAP/UART tasks are up (docs/ota-local-upload.md
            §2.3). Enabling this option lets the component schedule that
            confirmation itself (useful until the main/ hook lands).

    config BIRDIEBOT_OTA_AUTO_MARK_VALID_DELAY_MS
        int "Auto-confirm delay after boot (ms)"
        depends on BIRDIEBOT_OTA_AUTO_MARK_VALID
        default 10000
        range 1000 60000
        help
            Delay before the component calls wt_ota_mark_app_valid() when
            BIRDIEBOT_OTA_AUTO_MARK_VALID is enabled.

endmenu
